WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.254
Every word in a sentence has a job.

2
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:13.369
The job is called its word class.

3
00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.457
Let's meet four important ones.

4
00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:20.452
NOUNS name a person, place, thing or idea.

5
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:25.476
'dog' and 'bone' are nouns.

6
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.996
Test: can you put 'a' or 'the' in front? Yes!

7
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:40.022
More nouns: a person, a place, a thing, an idea.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.904
VERBS are doing or being words.

9
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.244
'ate' is the verb. It is what the dog did.

10
00:00:54.233 --> 00:00:57.252
Past, present, future. Only verbs can do that!

11
00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:02.834
Words like 'is' and 'was' are verbs too.

12
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:06.923
ADJECTIVES describe a noun.

13
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.083
'hungry' tells us about the dog.

14
00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:17.086
Swap it for another adjective. It still works!

15
00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.075
Test: does it fit in 'the ___ dog'?

16
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.878
ADVERBS describe a verb.

17
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:34.143
'quickly' tells us HOW the dog ate.

18
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.548
Adverbs tell us how, when or where.

19
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:48.530
Lots of adverbs end in -ly.

20
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.161
Now we know the job of each word!

21
00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.548
Watch out! One word can do different jobs.

22
00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:06.923
Here 'fish' is something I do. It is a verb.

23
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.408
Here 'fish' is a thing. It is a noun.

24
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.954
Look at the job the word does in the sentence.

25
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:21.023
Your turn! Pause the video now.

26
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:31.836
Let's check.

27
00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:39.280
How many did you get?

28
00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:48.053
Every word has a job. Look at what it does!
